From 802b25a6e258a5a6088426b993cbff41bb247e81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom <tom@getimpala.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:32:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Loader] Pinned staging for the Run:ai streamer path
 (env-gated) + weight checksum hook

Experiment 4 on an 8xB300 (Impala, 2026-10-11): the weight stage of a cold boot is bound by
PAGEABLE host->device copies. The Run:ai streamer preads into one pageable numpy buffer and
vLLM's weight_loaders then copy from it with param.copy_(), i.e. a driver-staged memcpy per
tensor (~2.4 GB/s per worker with 8 workers on this box, 4.5 GB/s alone).

This change page-locks the streamer's CPU buffer right after stream_files() (parallel
MADV_POPULATE_WRITE, then cudaHostRegister; ~0.2 s/GB) and, by default, streams every tensor
to the worker's GPU from pinned memory (device=cuda:<rank>) so the weight_loaders see GPU
tensors and all TP narrows are device-to-device. The buffer is bounded
(RUNAI_STREAMER_MEMORY_LIMIT defaults to 40e9 when unset) and unregistered when the iterator
closes; any failure falls back to the stock path with a warning.

Gates (all off by default): IMPALA_PINNED_LOADER=1, IMPALA_PINNED_GPU_YIELD=1,
IMPALA_PINNED_BUFFER_BYTES (16e9 was best: pin setup 3.5 s, no stream penalty),
IMPALA_PINNED_TOUCH_THREADS, IMPALA_PINNED_THP. IMPALA_WEIGHT_CHECKSUM=<dir> writes a per-rank
report hashing every GPU parameter/buffer after process_weights_after_loading (used to prove
bit-identical weights between the stock and the pinned path).

Measured on GLM-5.2-NVFP4 (433 GiB, 232k tensors), vLLM 0.20.2, runai-model-streamer 0.16.1,
4x TP=2 on 8xB300: "Model loading took" 39-42 s vs 75-79 s (-48 %), READY -32...-36 s per
replica, checksums identical, throughput unchanged. TP=8: -2...-4 s on 47 s (that shape is
bound by every rank reading the whole checkpoint, not by the copy path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
